        ":question/problem": "What is the value of $\\frac{2}{3}\\int_{4}^{16}\\frac{2}{\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right){log}_{4}\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=\\log_{4}\\left(\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)\\right).$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x \\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}}\\,\u27f9\\,\\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $4$ | $16$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}\\int_{4}^{16}\\frac{2}{\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right){log}_{4}\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ & =\\frac{4}{3}\\int_{4}^{16}\\frac{1}{{log}_{4}\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ & =\\frac{4}{3}\\int_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}4\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{4 \\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}}{3}\\int_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot\\left(2\\operatorname{ln}4(\\operatorname{ln}Abs(u))\\right)|_{1}^{2} \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot\\left(2\\operatorname{ln}4\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}2-\\operatorname{ln}1)\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot\\left(2\\operatorname{ln}({2}^{2})\\operatorname{ln}2\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot\\left(4{ln}^{2}2\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
